/**
 * CuriosityCraft 3D asset manifest (generated by the art-direction pass; scales were measured from each
 * file's bounding box, not guessed). All files live under web/public/assets/3d and are CC0 —
 * see ASSETS3D.md at the repo root for creators, sources and licences.
 *
 * Conventions
 *  - 1 unit ~ 1 metre. Humanoid characters are ~1.15 units tall, trees 3.5-5, landmarks 2-8.
 *  - `scale` is a uniform scale to apply to the loaded scene root.
 *  - `yOffset` (already multiplied by scale) lifts the model so its lowest point sits on y=0
 *    (or floats it: fish, bee, planet).
 *  - `animations` maps our verbs to the real clip names inside the file (THREE.AnimationClip.name).
 *  - `hide` lists mesh node names to set `visible=false` after loading (KayKit heroes ship with
 *    every weapon attached to their hands).
 *  - `tint` is an optional colour to multiply into the materials (clone materials first!) to
 *    re-theme a shared model (e.g. sandstone columns, coral made from crystals).
 *  - .gltf files reference a sibling .bin and shared PNG atlas; GLTFLoader resolves them relative
 *    to the url, so never move a .gltf without its neighbours.
 */
